      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10154406::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC6397024::web::017::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The unmodified alloy exhibits only mild or negligible irradiation hardening.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 5 at% Hf should be added to produce a quinary derivative of W38Ta36Cr15V11.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 5 at% Hf will suppress radiation-induced Cr/V-rich precipitation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10154406::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC10154406::web::017::high_tolerance_to_energetic_particle_irr"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf addition will make the alloy more suitable for practical bulk fabrication.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf atoms will be incorporated into the BCC solid solution and stabilize the BCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf will slow the segregation of Cr and V into second-phase precipitates.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf raises the energy barrier for atomic reordering and thereby lowers the diffusion mobility of Cr and V.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced Cr and V mobility will hinder precipitate nucleation and growth.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Solid-solution strengthening from Hf will preserve the alloy's hardness.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf addition will not introduce additional irradiation defects.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10154406::web::017::high_tolerance_to_energetic_particle_irr"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
